[gd_scene load_steps=2 format=3]

; The world check, on its own scene like the campaign check and the locale audit.
;
; check-campaign.ps1 asks whether a campaign folder is WELL FORMED. This asks whether the world in
; it can be WALKED: enter every place, look at what the facts leave standing on it, do every verb
; the author permitted, begin a fight and come back out of it into a map that is still there, take
; every road, read the quest log off the facts - and then save, reload, and prove every place comes
; back identically from base map + facts.
;
; That last line is the World layer's answer to the fairness sweep. You cannot chi-squared a town
; (PLACES_AND_PERSISTENCE.md section 10), so what correct means here is the validator plus the
; round trip, and this scene is the round trip.
;
; It needs no board, no tray and no dice - Content.World.Exploring is Godot-free on purpose, and
; this whole check is the proof of that. The one thing the scene is here for is the translation
; server, so a cue, a place name and a quest title can be read as a player would read them. Run it
; with check-world.ps1.

[ext_resource type="Script" path="res://Diagnostics/WorldCheck.cs" id="1_check"]

[node name="WorldCheck" type="Node"]
script = ExtResource("1_check")
